  data:  # f51a
    kind: work_item  # f51a
    title: "stamp_symbol_fingerprints retains every file's source+tree+index for the whole pass — group symbols by file and free per file"  # f51a
    status: todo_soft  # f51a
    priority: 2  # f51a
    parent:  # f51a
    tags:  # f51a
    - dogfood  # f51a
    - performance  # f51a
    isbefore: []  # f51a
    duplicate_of: []  # f51a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # f51a
    pr_ref:  # f51a
    description: "Follow-up to WI-balaf (PR #394). Two costs, one cause.\n\nMEASURED. On this monorepo, stamp_symbol_fingerprints holds at peak:\n    source_cache + tree_cache (pre-existing)   847 MB\n    _PyCoverIndex per file (added by #394)     226 MB   (83 bytes/AST node)\nover 1,126 python files and 2,865,626 AST nodes. Instrument: a per-file index build\nloop measuring ru_maxrss deltas; the numbers are peak RSS, not allocation counts.\n\nROOT CAUSE — the pass cannot finish with a file. stamp_symbol_fingerprints iterates\n`for sym in symbols` in whatever order the symbol list arrives, so a given file's\nsymbols are scattered through the iteration and nothing can ever be freed. Both\ncaches therefore grow monotonically to cover the ENTIRE repo, and #394's index\ninherits that lifetime.\n\nTHE FIX IS A REORDER, NOT A CACHE-EVICTION POLICY. Group symbols by (path,\nlanguage) first, process one file's symbols together, then drop that file's source,\ntree and index before moving to the next. Peak memory becomes O(largest file)\ninstead of O(repo), which is a reduction against the PRE-#394 baseline too, not just\nagainst the index I added.\n\nWHY THIS IS SAFE TO REORDER: each symbol is stamped independently from its own span\nagainst its own file's tree. No symbol's fingerprint depends on any other symbol or\non iteration order, so grouping cannot change any emitted value. That claim is\ncheckable the same way #394 was — scripts/compare-survey-fingerprints.py over a\nbefore/after survey should report 0 of ~42,543 changed, with no file edited between\nthe runs this time (the 1 change in #394's check was the edited file itself).\n\nWATCH FOR: `symbols` is typed Iterable[Symbol], so grouping materializes it. It is a\nlist in production (run_survey passes all_symbols), but the signature permits a\ngenerator and a caller relying on streaming would regress. Either narrow the type or\nmaterialize deliberately and say so.\n\nEXPECTED PAYOFF, honestly bounded: this is a memory item, not a latency one. Peak\nRSS should drop substantially on large repos; wall clock should be roughly neutral\n(one grouping sort added, the same trees built once each). If a measurement shows a\nlatency gain too, it would come from better cache locality, and that should be\nmeasured rather than assumed."  # f51a
    fields: {}  # f51a
