  message: "OWNER RULING (2026-08-17), verbatim: \"I guess we've mined all the processing\nefficiency that's reasonable to mine at this point in the hypergumbo project.\"\n\nPARKED — wont_do + someday. Not \"won't ever\"; \"not at this point in the project\".\nThis item is intact and its ceiling is measured, so re-opening is a status change,\nnot a re-derivation.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY MINED, so nobody re-measures it:\n  cold run_survey on this monorepo   517.7s -> 139.1s   (3.7x)\n    #394  fingerprint locator was quadratic in file size   -297.7s (62.6% of wall)\n    #395  --minimal declines side outputs a caller never reads   -59.1s\n    #397  one shared CLI scan instead of four                    -23.3s\n\nWHY PARKED — and note this is a MEMORY item, so parking it means accepting a\nmeasured cost, not declining a speedup. stamp_symbol_fingerprints holds every\nfile's source+tree+index for the whole pass: 847 MB pre-existing + 226 MB from\n#394's index (83 B/AST node) on this monorepo.\n\nTWO REASONS IT IS SAFE TO PARK. (a) Nothing has hit an OOM; the +27% rides on a\nretention pattern that predates #394. (b) It is now in TENSION with the only\nremaining parse-sharing idea: sharing fingerprint.py's parse with py.py's would\nREQUIRE holding trees across phases, i.e. more retention. Building both would be\nbuilding against oneself.\n\nRE-OPEN TRIGGER: an actual OOM or a repo whose AST-node total makes the +27%\ndecisive. The fix shape is recorded (group symbols by file, free per file) and\nwould cut the pre-existing 847 MB too."  # efe0
